# Ruta 10 (C4a, contract 39), 28 x 30. column = i, row = j. Ruta 9 arrives at the WEST edge of the NORTH half (i = 0, rows 6..7); the north half holds the healing center at the tunnel entrance (
# the Centro door c) and the north MOUTH of the Tunel Oscuro (23,2). A wall of cliff rows (j = 14..16) is the mountain: the way to the south half is the tunnel (its south mouth (6,17)); the road then leads to Pueblo
# Bruma at the SOUTH edge (i = 13..14, j = 29). Look: a rocky pass at the foot of a mountain: gravel, boulders, scree, cairns, cliff faces, a rope fence; signs warn that the tunnel is pitch dark.
@map ruta_10
@size 28 30
@interior no
@area ruta_10
@bg 0
@fill gravel
@surf yes     # C7 (contract 53): the lake of the Central Electrica (the plant is reached by surfing across it)
@spawn west 1 6 E
@spawn south 13 28 N
@spawn centro_door 9 5 S
@spawn tunnel_n 23 3 S
@spawn tunnel_s 6 18 S
@spawn lake_gate 22 18 S     # C7: back from the Central Electrica (the shore in front of the lake)
@encounters grass rate=15      # Route 10: the voltage ball is the common one, with the songbird, the snake and the sand mouse around it
  spoolt 19 23 45
  jabbird 19 22 20
  coilisp 19 22 35
@end
# Open ground (contract 63, normal route): a step onto plain ground (not tall grass, water, a door, a ledge, an arrow floor) rolls this table when rand8 < 4 (4/256 per step).
@open_rate 4
# Roaming wild creatures (contract 55, rollout in 63): 3 creatures of this table wander the open ground (not the tall grass); touching one starts that wild battle.
@roam 3 table=grass period=1800
@encounters water rate=10
  urchip 30 33 50
  skipgoby 30 33 30
  lazatee 31 33 20
@end
@legend
  D  object=central_door    # C7: the plant's service door in a rock face on the north shore of the lake, reachable only from the water (its other three neighbours are rocks)
  S  object=sign text=ruta10.lake.sign interact=look
